        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-56",
        "notes": "Checked both local steps and current Jensen, linearity, Fubini and product-law interfaces. Fixed-anchor score is bounded/integrable and has mean f(x)^T(mu_minus-mu_plus); convexity gives the positive-label bound for either loss. The ordered distinct-class law is symmetric because the iid product law and inequality event are symmetric. Swapping classes yields exactly the negative-label mean-classifier risk, so the uniform-label task average agrees. tau<1 is essential; tau=0 still permits distinct conditioning. Zero representations give equality. No choice, unattained classifier optimum or swapped sign error; reader/refuter no finding."
