      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-56",
        "notes": "Checked Proof 1.1–3.1 with current covariance, induced operator norm, product-law/Fubini, linearity, vector Cauchy–Schwarz and Jensen supplier statements. Every integrand is bounded on probability spaces. Conditional difference is centered with covariance 2 Sigma because both cross terms factor to zero. Jensen gives lower bound 1; E|score|<=sqrt(2||Sigma||)||f(x)|| gives c0=sqrt2 L0 after Lipschitz and collision-law averaging. tau=0 is handled separately and tau<1 allows distinct conditioning; no null-event conditional risk used. Zero anchor and covariance need no division. Reader/refuter have no finding. Source supplement A.1 is supporting context; constants are derived locally."
      },
