      "risk_review": {
        "status": "complete",
        "reviewer": "alpha-batch-56",
        "notes": "Checked Proof 1.1–4.1 and actual MGF, Markov, log, product-law/Fubini, linearity and Cauchy–Schwarz supplier statements. Independent centered projections give proxy 2R^2 sigma^2 and bounded score |q|<=2R^2. For sigma>0, Chernoff at t/(2R^2 sigma^2) gives epsilon/(3R^2) when R>=1 and epsilon/3 otherwise; multiplying by 1+2R^2 costs at most epsilon. sigma=0 is handled separately by arbitrary positive thresholds and a countable union, avoiding division by zero. gamma>=1 and positive-part scaling give the hinge bound; ordered-class symmetry identifies the uniform-label risk. R=1 formulas agree and epsilon=1 is valid. Logistic is expressly excluded. Reader/refuter no finding; source supplement A.2 and footnote 8 checked."
      },
