    "cor-subgaussian-contrastive-representation-transfer": {
      "citations": [
        {
          "fact": "A1",
          "source": "def-axiom-of-choice",
          "source_section": "Definition",
          "quote": "The **Axiom of Choice** (AC) is the following statement.\n\n> Every family of nonempty sets has a choice function\n> (Choice function).\n\nWritten out: for every set $\\mathcal{F}$ all of whose members are nonempty,\nthere exists a function $g$ with domain $\\mathcal{F}$ satisfying $g(S) \\in S$ for\nall $S \\in \\mathcal{F}$.\n\nAn equivalent formulation is that a product of nonempty sets is nonempty: if\n$X_i \\ne \\emptyset$ for every $i \\in I$, then $\\prod_{i \\in I} X_i \\ne \\emptyset$.\nHere $\\prod_{i \\in I} X_i$ is the set of functions $f$ with domain $I$ such that\n$f(i) \\in X_i$ for every $i \\in I$; when a family of nonempty sets is indexed by\nitself, such an $f$ is precisely a choice function for it.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "A1",
          "source": "thm-contrastive-representation-transfer-under-within-class-deviation",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and the one-negative latent-class model with $\\tau<1$. Fix either source hinge or logistic loss, $M\\ge1$, and a measurable exact empirical minimizer $\\widehat f\\in\\mathcal F$ satisfying $\\widehat L_{\\rm un}(\\widehat f)\\le\\widehat L_{\\rm un}(g)$ for every $g\\in\\mathcal F$ almost surely, under the measurability hypotheses of the uniform-generalization result. For each comparator $f\\in\\mathcal F$ and every $0<\\delta<1$, with probability at least $1-\\delta$ over the IID triplet sample,\n\n$$L_{\\rm sup}(\\widehat f)\\le L^\\mu_{\\rm sup}(\\widehat f)\\le L^\\ne_{\\rm un}(f)+\\frac{\\sqrt2L_0\\tau s(f)+2\\Gamma_M(S,\\delta)}{1-\\tau},$$\n\nwhere $L_{\\rm sup}$ is the infimum of the average binary-task risk over all linear classifiers, $s(f)$ is the within-class covariance deviation, and\n\n$$\\Gamma_M(S,\\delta):=\\frac{2\\sqrt{18}L_0R\\,\\mathcal R_S(\\mathcal F)}{M}+3B_{\\ell,R}\\sqrt{\\frac{\\ln(4/\\delta)}{2M}}$$\n\nis the uniform-deviation quantity for the same sample and loss. The event is simultaneous for all comparators.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F1",
          "source": "thm-contrastive-representation-transfer-under-within-class-deviation",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Assume the Axiom of Choice and the one-negative latent-class model with $\\tau<1$. Fix either source hinge or logistic loss, $M\\ge1$, and a measurable exact empirical minimizer $\\widehat f\\in\\mathcal F$ satisfying $\\widehat L_{\\rm un}(\\widehat f)\\le\\widehat L_{\\rm un}(g)$ for every $g\\in\\mathcal F$ almost surely, under the measurability hypotheses of the uniform-generalization result. For each comparator $f\\in\\mathcal F$ and every $0<\\delta<1$, with probability at least $1-\\delta$ over the IID triplet sample,\n\n$$L_{\\rm sup}(\\widehat f)\\le L^\\mu_{\\rm sup}(\\widehat f)\\le L^\\ne_{\\rm un}(f)+\\frac{\\sqrt2L_0\\tau s(f)+2\\Gamma_M(S,\\delta)}{1-\\tau},$$\n\nwhere $L_{\\rm sup}$ is the infimum of the average binary-task risk over all linear classifiers, $s(f)$ is the within-class covariance deviation, and\n\n$$\\Gamma_M(S,\\delta):=\\frac{2\\sqrt{18}L_0R\\,\\mathcal R_S(\\mathcal F)}{M}+3B_{\\ell,R}\\sqrt{\\frac{\\ln(4/\\delta)}{2M}}$$\n\nis the uniform-deviation quantity for the same sample and loss. The event is simultaneous for all comparators.",
          "uses": [
            "1.1",
            "2.1"
          ]
        },
        {
          "fact": "F2",
          "source": "lem-subgaussian-contrastive-margin-comparison",
          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "In the one-negative latent-class model, fix a bounded representation $f$ with $\\sup_x\\|f(x)\\|_2\\le R$, where $R>0$. Use the hinge loss $\\ell_{\\rm h}(t)=(1+t)_+$. Suppose that for every class $c$, the centered vector $f(X)-\\mu_c$, for $X\\sim D_c$, is sub-Gaussian in every direction with proxy $\\sigma^2\\ge0$. For $0<\\epsilon\\le1$, define\n\n$$\\gamma:=\\begin{cases}1+2R\\sigma\\sqrt{2\\ln R+\\ln(3/\\epsilon)},&R\\ge1,\\\\1+2R\\sigma\\sqrt{\\ln(3/\\epsilon)},&0<R<1.\\end{cases}$$\n\nThen the contrastive risk conditioned on distinct positive and negative classes satisfies\n\n$$L^\\ne_{\\rm un}(f)\\le\\gamma L^\\mu_{\\gamma,\\rm sup}(f)+\\epsilon.$$\n\nThis comparison is for the hinge contrastive loss and its scaled hinge mean-classifier risk.",
          "uses": [
            "2.1"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "derivations": [
        {
          "id": "derivation-1.1",
